

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 8

                                  FOR

                               BRADIPO I







          Alessio Albertoni
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  "It is a political error to practice deceit, if deceit is carried too 
far."
  -Frederick II, King of Prussia, 1740.


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  Winter gave way to spring, and Bradipo I made ready to carry out his 
imperial orders.  He assigned the 207th Eagles, the 76th Eagles, the 31st 
Legion and the 289th Phalanx to Ambrosius in Kiska.
  With the advent of the early summer season Bradipo I's Skeletal Army spell 
fizzled and Bradipo I was left with his face covered with psycho-kinetic 
goo.
  In late summer, Bradipo I announced a call for volunteers in Kiska and was 
able to form the 79th Eagles to fight for Bradipo I.
  The hot days of summer surrendered to fall.  Bradipo I boldly marched his 
forces into Katmai (#108).  Southeast of here lies the prosperous province 
of Donegal (#209), ruled by Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango.  It is known 
to be a Sea province occupied by no races.  Viewing the southwestern 
horizon, one can see a Sea province called the Mirkwood Sea (#109).  It is 
said that Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango is the ruler there.  It is known 
to be populated by no races.  To the west there is a Forest province known 
as Black Forest (#1808), a land of Trolls where Agesilao rules.  They can 
muster an army of Trolls to defend their territory.

  An army coming from the empire of Bradipo I invaded Katmai, hoping to 
conquer that province ruled by Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) and 
made up of extensive Forests.  Bradipo I commanded the attacking armies.  
The defending forces were led by Alain (#33).  The armies were drawn up into 
lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Katmai (0108):

  32nd/V   306th/V   210th/A    79th/G  
  Lt Cav    Lt Cav    Camels    Eagles  
