  DEFENDING ARMY

  Bradipo I commanded a host of loyal soldiers.  Standing tall with his 
warriors was Alain.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Babba Sissoko (#0) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Alain (#33) strode forward and challenged Bradipo I to 
personal combat.  Bradipo I declined to enter personal combat.
  The forces commanded by Bradipo I were disappointed by his cowardice.  
They grimly marched on, though with shaken confidence.  His luck appeared to 
be on furlough, as the engagement's unforeseen timing caught his men 
somewhat unprepared.  Alain's forces thus obtained a significant edge.  On 
the other hand in this perilous slugging match, Bradipo I appeared to gain 
the tactical upper hand.

  On the left outside flank, the Veteran 32nd Light Cavalry were arrayed 
against the 291st Trolls.  The 271st Dragons swooped down on the 32nd 
Light Cavalry and attacked without mercy.
  Alain maneuvered the 271st Dragons to the front line, angling for a better 
nemesis effect.  The nervous horses of the 32nd Light Cavalry were spooked 
by the howls of the fearsome Beasts they were faced with.  The 32nd 
Light Cavalry battled with the 271st Dragons and had their booties kicked 
all the way up their throats.
  In the interior lines, the Veteran 306th Light Cavalry were arrayed 
against the Crack 137th Skeletal Phalanx.  The 335th Dragons soared over the 
306th Light Cavalry and attacked them.
  Alain maneuvered the 335th Dragons to the front line, angling for a 
superior match-up.  The nervous horses of the 306th Light Cavalry were 
frightened by the nasty smell of the Beasts they beheld.  The 306th 
Light Cavalry battled the 335th Dragons and were cut down like cattle.
  Within the interior lines, the 210th Camel Corps were joined by a troop of 
the Order of Knights Hospitaller, who exhorted them to fanaticism with their 
Good and righteous fury.  They were arrayed against the 281st Trolls.  The 
304th Dragons swooped down on the 210th Camel Corps and attacked them.  The 
210th Camel Corps battled the 281st Trolls and were sliced and diced like a 
knife cutting through butter.
  On the right flank, the Green 79th Eagles were arrayed against the Veteran 
309th Legion.  The 79th Eagles swooped down on the 309th Legion and attacked 
them.  The 126th Skeletal Dragons soared over the 79th Eagles and attacked 
them.  The 79th Eagles fought the 309th Legion and had their booties kicked 
up their throats.
  Alain's great horde overwhelmed the army of Bradipo I and took the field, 
dispersing their enemies.  The 271st Dragons annihilated the 32nd 
Light Cavalry.  The 335th Dragons demolished the 306th Light Cavalry.  The 
281st Trolls slew the 210th Camel Corps almost to a man.  The 309th Legion 
scattered the 79th Eagles in all directions.
  The defenders turned back Bradipo I's forces and drove them out of Katmai. 
His forces completely destroyed, Bradipo I escaped frightened and alone to 
Kiska.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded the province of Kaluga, a 
Plain area ruled by Bradipo I.  Kaluga was conquered and occupied by Rainulf 
(#25)'s host.  Rainulf leads approximately 4 Garrison.
  Ambrosius commanded the 31st Legion, the 76th Eagles, the 207th Eagles and 
the 289th Phalanx to remain in Big Sky with the provincial garrison 
commander.  Bradipo I inherited the Feather of the Great Eagle.  Ambrosius 
went back to Valhalla, having tried his best to execute his assignments.

  The fall season cooled into the stillness of early winter.  Bradipo I 
journeyed to Khalturin.  Viewing the southeastern horizon, a man can see a 
Desert province known as Kerry (#309).  It is said that 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango reigns there.  It is known to be occupied 
by Dwarves.  Their Dwarven fighters fight in the style of Camel Corps and 
Fleet.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Bradipo I for this year.


  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Drago (#39) arose one day with a desire to see Cantia, and so left Big Sky 
to travel to that province.
  Tilden (#47) grew bored with the scenery in Kiska and departed for Abu 
Matariq.
  Brunhilda (#86) left Transylvania to preside over a reunion of her old 
battalion in Katmai.


  Here is the financial report for Bradipo I's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 46 gold in revenue.  2 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  12 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Bradipo I was left 
with 100 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Adele
To: Bradipo I

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I travelled to Mongu.
  During early summer, I levied the 45th Legion and the 49th Legion in Mongu 
to serve me.
  Midsummer's day passed and a hot late summer came.  Adele's attempted cast 
of the Plague spell was unsuccessful.  My efforts improved my aptitude in 
Necromancy.
  With the coming of the fall season I marched my forces into Moongard 
(#405).  To the east there is a Desert province known as Trouthome (#505), a 
prosperous land of Elves where Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango reigns.  
Their Elven fighters traditionally fight as Phalanx.
  Adele's forces fought in a battle in Moongard, but a foreign general 
commanded it.  The battle is in the General Intelligence Report.
  During early winter, I could not cast Tornado on Trouthome because I 
needed to be in or next to the target province.  So, I practiced my Meleeing 
well, and even consulted a palm reader, but could not improve my Meleeing.

  Thy humble servant,   Adele


From: Indra
To: Bradipo I

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter gave way to spring, and I prepared to carry out my urgent 
assignments.  I tried to improve my Sageness, but the task seemed beyond my 
aptitude.  I invented nothing in my sagely experiments.
  With the advent of the early summer season, I tried to improve my Sageness,
but the task seemed beyond my ability.  I discovered nothing worthy of note 
in my sagely researches.
  With the advent of the late summer season, in my sagely researches, I 
discovered a fabulous invention called the Flood Dams!  The following 
benefits are conferred by the Flood Dams:
  Flood Dams reduce the effects of the Flood spell used by Elemental 
Magicians.  When it's cast on a province owned by your kingdom, affected 
armies currently in the target province will immediately lose one movement 
point.

  In fall, I invented nothing valuable in my sagely experiments.
  With the coming of the early winter season I discovered nothing in my 
sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Indra


From: Ambrosius
To: Bradipo I

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter melted into sweet spring, and I made ready to carry out my 
urgent assignments.  I tried a Tornado spell, but bungled it.  A mysterious 
magical counterspell seemed to have impeded my spell.
  In early summer, I rode my flying armies over to Kaluga.  Turning to the 
east, one espies a Plain area, which is known as Rosehaven (#407).  It is 
populated by Humans and Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango rules there.  Their 
Human warriors array themselves as Axemen.  Southeast of here is Siouxhome 
(#308), a prosperous Desert area ruled by Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango, 
where Humans dwell.  Their Human warriors array themselves as Camel Corps.  
I found a feature in Kaluga: a Catacombs (#56) inhabited by the Mummy.  What 
treasure may lie there is unknown.  The Mummy is a horribly strong undead 
Pharoah of ancient times which has been wrapped in linen bandages and laid 
to rest, but cannot pass to the next world because of some terrible misdeed 
committed by the Pharoah in his lifetime.

  Soldiers carrying the battle-standards of the Bradipo Iian empire marched 
on the Plain province of Kaluga, a land garrisoned by the soldiers of 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0).  I commanded the attacking armies.  
The defending forces were commanded by Migfox (#65).  The armies were drawn 
up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Kaluga (0307):

  207th                       
  Eagles                      
