  DEFENDING ARMY

  I led my armies into the fray.  Standing at the ready with his warriors 
was Migfox.
  I strode forward and challenged Migfox to personal combat.  Migfox 
declined to enter combat.
  The forces commanded by Migfox were dismayed by his faint-heartedness.  
They marched on, though with shaken confidence.  Ambrosius's luck didn't 
hold up this time.  My superstitious men became unsettled when my priests 
were unable to properly sacrifice a bull to the Great Father because they 
had all been stolen by racketeers.  On the other hand tactical superiority 
was clearly assured by my unmatched tactical mind.

  On the left outside wing, the 76th Eagles faced the Veteran 336th 
Light Cavalry.  The 76th Eagles soared over the 336th Light Cavalry and 
attacked without mercy.  The 207th Eagles swooped down on the 336th 
Light Cavalry and attacked them.  The 76th Eagles battled with the 336th 
Light Cavalry and determinedly plowed into their opponents.
  Within the interior lines, the Crack 31st Legion sang out their fiery 
battle hymns, inspired with a spirit of fanatical elan by their exalted 
King.  They were arrayed against the 263rd Legion.  The 31st Legion fought 
the 263rd Legion and smashed them like rotten oranges.
  Out on the right flank, the Crack 289th Phalanx sang out their battle 
hymns, infused with a holy, fanatical elan by their exalted King.  They 
faced the 337th Light Cavalry.  The 289th Phalanx fought with the 337th 
Light Cavalry and aggressively knifed into them.
  Having found a vulnerable point in the line of the host of Babba Sissoko 
(#0), a final savage slashing attack defeated their opponent and won the 
battle for me.  The 31st Legion annihilated the 263rd Legion.  The 76th 
Eagles chased after the enemy and scattered the 336th Light Cavalry in all 
directions.  The 207th Eagles overtook the enemy in their panicky retreat 
and demolished the 337th Light Cavalry.
  Kaluga was overrun by the forces of Ambrosius.  The battle affected the 
quality of our forces:  the mayhem wreaked by the 207th Eagles during the 
battle has elevated the spirits of its warriors, and it has achieved Veteran 
quality.  His forces completely destroyed, Migfox (#65) fled alone to 
Khalturin.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer came.  I flew into Big Sky.  
Turning to the east, one can see a Sea area, which is known as the Io Sea 
(#406).  It is populated by no races and no one rules there.  I located a 
previously unheard of Tomb (#90) in Big Sky, held by the Banshee.  What 
treasure may lie there is unknown.  The Banshee is the undead spirit of an 
evil female elf.  Its horrible scream can strike a man dead.

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Bradipo Iian empire marched 
on the Mountain province of Big Sky, a land garrisoned by the soldiers of 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0).  Ambrosius's forces experienced 
little opposition in Big Sky and I there established our reign.  Big Sky was 
discovered to have a tax base of 5 gold.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into fall.  I found a feature in Big Sky: 
an Ancient Megaliths (#45) inhabited by the Beholder.  Legend says the 
Feather of the Great Eagle is hidden here.  The Beholder is a floating 
gaseous globule with many eyes, each eye capable of casting a potent spell.  
I girded my weapon and entered the Ancient Megaliths cautiously.  I 
encountered the Beholder.  Rotating one of its 10 eyestalks toward me, 
the Beholder gave off a fiery beam, impacting with the power of a Psychic 
Blast spell, projecting psychic waves of stunning force towards me.  I was 
stunned and staggered around at random.  Turning one of its eyes toward me, 
the Beholder emitted a beam, impacting with the power of a Telekinetic Storm 
spell and scorched me with 9 damage points.  Some small objects zipped 
towards the Beholder and damaged the Beholder, inflicting 2 damage points.  
I stood dazed, stunned out of my mind.

  The Beholder advanced to bow range.  I could do nothing in my stunned 
state.
  The Beholder charged into melee range.  The stun wore off and I prepared 
to attack.  The Beholder summoned all its strength and bravely struck at its 
fearsome enemy but I evaded the fangs.  I invoked my Antennae of Psychic 
Blasting, projecting psychic waves of stunning force towards the Beholder.  
Unfortunately, the Antennae of Psychic Blasting used up its last charge.  It 
crumbled to dust and merged with the sands of time.  With amazing speed, I 
thrust at the Beholder and damaged the Beholder, inflicting 4 damage points. 
In its pathetic stunned state, the Beholder could not determine what to do.
  I circled right and attacked the Beholder but my sword whiffed harmlessly 
through the air.  The Beholder stood stunned, unable to regain its balance.  
I swang at the Beholder and scored on the Beholder, doing 9 points of 
damage.  Now the effects of the stun wore off and the Beholder prepared to 
renew its attack.  I deftly swang at the Beholder and scored on the Beholder,
doing 8 points of damage.  The Beholder staggered, stunned by the force of 
the mortal blow.  I turned my attention to the hoard of the Beholder.  I 
bagged the Feather of the Great Eagle.  I examined the Feather of the Great 
Eagle and discovered the following properties:
  The Feather of the Great Eagle gives the bearer the power of command over 
eagles:  when encountering a eagle in its lair, the treasure is taken 
without a fight merely by using the TA-lk tactic.  When the bearer leads an 
army into battle, any unled eagles in adjacent provinces will fight on his 
side, and then fly home.  If he invades a eagle province, an average of 33% 
of the eagles will defect to his side.  This defection rate is halved 
against player-led eagles.
  I took 4 gold from the treasure trove of the Beholder.
  While scouting the Ancient Megaliths, I saw a Pentagram which seemed to be 
of a magical nature.
  Magic runes formed on the Pentagram, saying "The Pentagram changes your 
sex from male to female (or vice versa.)  By the power of the Pentagram, I 
zap you from female to male!  How do you like the improvement?  Har har har! !!"
  I commanded the 31st Legion, the 76th Eagles, the 207th Eagles and the 
289th Phalanx to remain in Big Sky with the provincial garrison commander.  
Bradipo I inherited the Feather of the Great Eagle.  I went back to 
Valhalla, having tried my best to execute my assignments.


  Thy humble servant,   Ambrosius


