  DEFENDING ARMY

  Adele commanded a host of loyal soldiers.  Tarsus (#43) marched with his 
loyal troops, jaws set in grim resolution.  Tlazolteotl (#88) stood 
determinedly at the head of her thousands.
  Tlazolteotl stepped forward and challenged Tarsus (#43) to honorable 
combat.  Tarsus accepted the challenge to personal combat.  The forces 
commanded by Tarsus were disheartened by his death, yet still they moved 
forward with some hope of victory.  Adele assumed command of the forces of 
the realm of Bradipo I.  Her luck seemed to be on furlough, as the 
engagement's unforeseen timing caught her men somewhat unprepared.  
Tlazolteotl (#88)'s men thus obtained a considerable edge.  Also, it soon 
became clear that Adele was tactically outmatched by Tlazolteotl.  
Tlazolteotl maneuvered her forces with great sagacity.
  Tarsus (#43) was frustrated by the Dragons, who could not comprehend his 
commands.
  Out on the left outside wing, the Elite 25th Legion were arrayed against 
the Crack 139th Phalanx.  The 46th Dragons soared over the 75th Dragons and 
attacked without mercy.  The unwieldy formation of the 139th Phalanx was 
shaken by the flexible Legionnaires.  The 256th Dragons swooped down on the 
45th Legion and attacked without mercy.  The 75th Dragons swooped down on 
the 46th Dragons and attacked them.
  Tlazolteotl (#88) maneuvered the 256th Dragons to the front line, as a 
strategem for a better nemesis effect.  The 25th Legion fought the 256th 
Dragons and was forced to retreat in disorder.
  Out on the right flank, the Crack 23rd Legion faced the Crack 222nd 
Phalanx.  The 158th Dragons soared over the 106th Dragons and attacked them. 
The clumsy mass of the 222nd Phalanx was shaken by the flexible 
Legionnaires.  The unwieldy mass of the 223rd Phalanx was severely tested by 
the maneuverable Legionnaires.  The 106th Dragons swooped down on the 158th 
Dragons and attacked without mercy.
  Tlazolteotl switched the 106th Dragons to the front line, angling for a 
better match-up.  The 23rd Legion battled with the 106th Dragons and was 
powerless to halt their advance.
  The forces of Tlazolteotl broke through the lines of their opposition and 
were victorious.  The 256th Dragons annihilated the 25th Legion.  The 106th 
Dragons destroyed the 23rd Legion.  The 75th Dragons scattered the 46th 
Dragons in all directions.  The 106th Dragons overtook the enemy and slew 
the 45th Legion almost to a man.  The 75th Dragons gave chase and demolished 
the 49th Legion.  The attacking Kingdom was defeated and turned back in its 
attempt to take Moongard.  Her forces completely destroyed, Adele escaped 
frightened and alone to Mongu.  The acting commander pulled back to Shasta 
with its command.
  In spring, Marlon (#68) moved into Macondo.  During his travels this 
season, a Renegade Swordsman unexpectedly rushed at Marlon from out of 
nowhere.  Marlon raised his arms, meaning to cast a Telekinetic Storm spell, 
but it backfired and a dove tumbled out of his hat instead.  
The Renegade Swordsman moved into bow range.  Gesturing with his arms, 
Marlon juxtaposed otherworldly forces of magic, casting a Charm spell.  
Marlon befriended the Renegade Swordsman and used his respite to get away.
  In late summer, Marlon moved into Orielle.

Kingdom of Kahn (#6):
  In spring, Hume (#77) rode into Transylvania.
  In early summer, Brunhilda (#86) informed Hume (#77) that Brunhilda (#86) 
would not sell her services for less than 4 gold.
  In fall, Hume (#77) travelled to Macondo.  During her travels this season, 
Hume was confronted by a Chimera.  Hoping to escape from her vicious 
opponent, Hume ran like the wind.  But Hume was too tired and, even with 
great effort, could not gain any ground on the Chimera.  The Chimera moved 
to bow range.  The Chimera breathed a flame breath at Hume and missed.  
The Chimera breathed a flame breath at Hume but his flame breath whiffed 
through the air.  Weaving her artful words of magic into a mighty 
Spiritwrack spell, Hume gestured with her arms, to make the Chimera quake 
and shiver with spiritual convulsions.  Incanting an Invisibility spell, 
Hume channelled scintillating, writhing strands of magic, fading into 
invisibility.  The Chimera charged into the melee.  The Chimera snapped at 
Hume and inflicted 2 damage points on Hume.  Hume thought to attempt a 
Fireball spell, but couldn't find a needed material component before Hume 
could make her spellcast.  The Chimera daringly snapped at Hume but Hume 
evaded the blow.  Her spell was disrupted by the event.  The Chimera then 
lunged at Hume and damaged Hume, inflicting 1 damage points.  Hume 
immediately thrust at the Chimera but her aim was just off.  The Chimera 
treacherously snapped at Hume and inflicted 6 damage points.  Showing no 
fear, Hume swang at the Chimera and scored on the Chimera, inflicting 4 
points of damage.  Hume maneuvered for a better attacking position.  Then 
Hume swang at the Chimera and walloped the Chimera with 5 damage points.  
The Chimera pretended to panic, then pivoted and arrogantly snapped at Hume 
and inflicted 3 damage points on Hume.  Hume dropped to the ground, mortally 
pierced.  And so it came to pass that Hume met her unseemly end.


